# iceland-device 0.28-9 - OWNER DECISION (proposed, shipped as its own file so that it can be dropped alone):
# Fedora's ABRT crash reporting daemons off. Five units ran on the installed system (field report 14 Oct 2026);
# the owner disabled them there by hand. Crash data is not lost: systemd-coredump stays on (coredumpctl list /
# coredumpctl info) and kernel oopses stay in the journal; what goes is ABRT's own collection, its GNOME
# notifications and its reporting (FAF / Bugzilla) - reports that Fedora cannot use for kernel-iceland anyway.
# Sorts before Fedora's 90-default.preset ("enable abrtd.service ..."), so "disable" wins; applied once per system
# like 50-iceland-unused.preset (marker /var/lib/iceland/.preset-unused-0.28-9).
disable abrtd.service
disable abrt-journal-core.service
disable abrt-oops.service
disable abrt-vmcore.service
disable abrt-xorg.service
